  "decision_summary": "The query is a tetrabenazine-like lactam with a verapamil-like dimethoxyphenyl/amine side chain. Direct tetrabenazine analogs show very low oral bioavailability (<10%), while valbenazine and noscapine show ~30–49%. The closest core analog and the extensive first-pass metabolism expected from the tertiary amine/dimethoxyphenyl motifs favor F < 20%, so the prediction is low.",
